  - m_Id: 2468837708587008
    m_Localized: "Verbs in the 3rd person singular of the past simple tense can have
      one of two endings: -o, -\u0117. The ending determines the verb type and how
      the verb form changes."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2468936236982272
    m_Localized: Busi Busi
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2470580639031296
    m_Localized: The past frequent tense describes an action that was repeated two
      or more times. The -ti suffix is replaced with the -dav- suffix, followed by
      endings.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2470839788298240
    m_Localized: Busi Daz
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2512098565349376
    m_Localized: The translation is shown at the top. Build the Lithuanian word from
      the letters below by tapping them (buttons can be tapped as many times as needed).
      Back removes the last letter, Check submits your answer, Next skips the word
      if you can't recall it (counts as a mistake). Each word is one of a verb's
      three forms (infinitive, present tense, and past tense). Get one wrong, or
      hit Next, and all three forms of that verb come back later to try again. Answer
      all three forms correctly to score points.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2530852363886592
    m_Localized: Great!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2539415870169088
